## CVAE Architecture (exact, do not change hidden dims)
- Year condition: c = one_hot(year, num_classes=5) ∈ ℝ^5
- Encoder input: concat(x, c) ∈ ℝ^22  →  Linear(22,128) → ReLU → Linear(128,160) → mu(80), logvar(80)
- Decoder input: concat(z, c) ∈ ℝ^85  →  Linear(85,128) → ReLU → Linear(128,17) → Sigmoid
- Latent dim L = 80
- beta = 1.0

## CVAE Reparameterization (Phase A3)
z = mu + sigma * eps
eps ~ N(0, I_L)
sigma = sqrt(exp(log_sigma_squared))

In PyTorch:
    # Encoder receives concatenated (x, c)
    xc = torch.cat([x, c], dim=-1)          # (batch, 21)
    mu, logvar = encoder(xc)                 # each (batch, 80)
    std = torch.exp(0.5 * logvar)
    eps = torch.randn_like(std)
    z = mu + std * eps                       # (batch, 80)
    # Decoder receives concatenated (z, c)
    zc = torch.cat([z, c], dim=-1)          # (batch, 85)
    x_hat = decoder(zc)                     # (batch, 17)

## CVAE Loss (Phase A3)
recon_loss = F.mse_loss(x_hat, x, reduction='sum') / N
kl_loss = -0.5 * torch.sum(1 + logvar - mu.pow(2) - logvar.exp()) / N
total_loss = recon_loss + beta * kl_loss   # beta = 1.0

## Post-Augmentation Temporal Reconstruction (Phase A3 — mandatory)
# After generating 650 rows each with (county, year) labels:
df_augmented = df_augmented.sort_values(['county', 'year']).reset_index(drop=True)
# Verify per county: 5 year groups × 5 samples = 25 rows per county
assert all(df_augmented.groupby('county').size() == 25)
# This sorted structure is what STGNN temporal windows are built from

## STGNN Node Features — F=5 (NOT raw 17 features)
# PCA compressed 17 → 4 pillars. The STGNN receives pillar space, not feature space.
NODE_FEATURES = 5   # [S_1, S_2, S_3, S_4, lag_score]
# Pillar scores come from pillar_scores_augmented.csv (650 rows)
# Lag score: (y_{i,t-1} - y_bar) / sigma_y, standardized over training scores

## STGNN Training — 25 Graph Snapshots (NOT 5)
# Augmentation creates 5 variants per year × 5 years = 25 training graphs
# Each graph: 26 nodes, fixed edges, node features from one (year, variant) pair
# Variants are NOT extra timesteps — they are augmented versions of the same year
# Temporal sequence per variant: [2021,2022,2023,2024] → predict 2025
# Evaluation: real snapshots only (variant_id=0), never on synthetic variants

## STGNN Architecture (exact layer counts from paper Figure 2)
- Spatial: 2× GCNConv layers (in=5, hidden=64), ReLU, Dropout(0.2)
- Temporal: 4 linear layers forming Q,K,V projections (d_key=32, d_val=32)
- Head: Linear(32,16) → ReLU → Linear(16,1)
- Total learnable layers = 9

## Training Config
- Optimizer: Adam, lr=1e-3, weight_decay=1e-4
- Epochs: 500 (both Phase A7 and A7b)
- Loss: MSE + L2 regularization (lambda=1e-4)

## Phase A7 — Evaluation Training (honest metrics)
- Train years: 2021-2024 (all 5 variants = 20 input snapshots), Test: 2025 real only
- Saves: models/stgnn_eval_weights.pt
- Reports: R², MAE, MSE on held-out 2025 real snapshot → displayed in View 5

## Phase A7b — Full Retraining (forecasting model)
- Train with ALL observed years available to the final model: for each variant, use [2021, 2022, 2023, 2024] → 2025, including the real 2025 target that A7 held out
- Same architecture and hyperparameters as A7, only data split changes
- Saves: models/stgnn_forecast_weights.pt
- Used by: ALL forecasting (A8), uncertainty (A9), counterfactuals (A10), Views 1-4
- NEVER report A7b metrics as "test performance" — there is no test set

## After Each Phase — Always Print
print(f"[Phase AX] Complete. Output shape: {output.shape}. Key stats: ...")
